WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.160
President Donald J. Trump has built a strong economy and is revitalizing the American dream.

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:08.480
He will go down as the greatest housing president in history.

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:10.760
America was built one home at a time.

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:11.820
I believe that.

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:14.540
Because the American dream was never just an idea.

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:20.100
It was a front door, a set of keys, a place where families built their future.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:25.700
For generations, homeownership meant security, independence, and stability.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:29.680
But today, that dream feels out of reach for too many Americans.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.280
Not because they stopped working hard, but because the system stopped working for them.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.080
That's why protecting housing matters.

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:41.340
Why institutions like Fannie Mae matter.

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:44.540
Working with banks so lending doesn't stop.

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:49.380
Capital keeps moving and people aren't locked out because their past wasn't perfect.

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:53.540
When banks can say yes, families can move forward.

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:58.080
The all new Fannie Mae, protector of the American dream.
